		{"id":"168402ba0f8c171f","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.1 Road to Cathedral - Cold plaines.md","x":13120,"y":-270,"width":1160,"height":1660},
		{"id":"3ed08fdbdc665568","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.3 Encounter between the woods n field.md","x":17180,"y":-420,"width":840,"height":1580,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"336084bba5a60f7f","type":"text","text":"### 💀 **Cursed Relic: The Mourner's Cameo**\n\n_Wondrous Item (necklace), rare (requires attunement)_\n\n> A small, tarnished silver locket shaped like a teardrop. The front bears the face of a weeping woman, her eyes closed in sorrow. Inside is a faded charcoal sketch of a child, name long eroded.\n\n---\n\n**Properties (when attuned):**\n\n- While wearing this locket, the bearer can cast **_Speak with Dead_** once per day, but only on corpses who died in grief, betrayal, or loneliness.\n    \n- Once per long rest, the wearer may also **turn invisible for 1 minute**, but only if no allies are within 10 feet.\n    \n\n---\n\n**Curse:**\n\n> The cameo feeds on isolation.\n\n- If the wearer **spends more than one hour alone**, they gain **temporary advantage on Insight and Perception checks**.\n    \n- But **if they remain with companions too long**, the locket begins to _whisper_ softly, urging betrayal and solitude.\n    \n\nAt the end of each long rest, roll a **DC 15 Wisdom saving throw**:\n\n- **Fail:** The wearer gains **1 level of exhaustion** and has **disadvantage on Persuasion checks** for the day.\n    \n- **Pass:** No ill effect, but they feel emotionally _numbed_.\n    \n\nRemoving the locket after attuning to it **requires a _Remove Curse_ spell** or destroying it in consecrated fire.\n\n---\n\nThe statue’s face shifts _slightly_ after the locket is lifted—its stone eyes now _open_ and full of sadness.","x":17180,"y":1418,"width":840,"height":682,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"cfb0c16619d0e6b2","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.4 Fields of Misery.md","x":18280,"y":-420,"width":880,"height":1580},
		{"id":"f8ba3742e2cce378","type":"text","text":"## 💀 The Mourning Plowman\n\n_Medium undead, neutral, cursed ghost of a farmer who died in grief_\n\n---\n\n**Armor Class** 12 (spectral body)  \n**Hit Points** 45 (6d8 + 18)  \n**Speed** 30 ft., can hover 5 ft. above ground\n\n---\n\n**STR** 14 (+2)  \n**DEX** 12 (+1)  \n**CON** 16 (+3)  \n**INT** 10 (+0)  \n**WIS** 14 (+2)  \n**CHA** 13 (+1)\n\n---\n\n**Saving Throws** Wis +4  \n**Skills** Insight +4, Nature +2, Religion +2  \n**Damage Resistances** necrotic, cold, nonmagical weapons  \n**Damage Immunities** poison  \n**Condition Immunities** charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned  \n**Senses** darkvision 60 ft., passive Perception 12  \n**Languages** Common, whispers in old dialects\n\n---\n\n### TRAITS\n\n**Bound to the Field.**  \nThe Plowman cannot willingly leave the Fields of Misery. If forcibly moved 100 feet beyond his current location, he vanishes and reforms the next dusk unless his curse is lifted.\n\n**Restless Duty.**  \nEach round that the Plowman is not in combat or interacting with someone, he mechanically plows the earth. If uninterrupted for 3 rounds, his spectral plow carves a **\"Runic Furrow\"** in a 10 ft. line: difficult terrain for others, healing him 5 HP.\n\n**Ethereal Form.**  \nThe Plowman can partially phase through objects and terrain, gaining advantage on Dexterity saving throws made to move through or around environmental hazards.\n\n---\n\n### ACTIONS\n\n**Rustbite Plow (Melee Weapon Attack):**  \n_+4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target._  \nHit: 9 (2d6 + 2) slashing damage. On a failed DC 12 Strength save, the target is **knocked prone** by the dragging weight of the spectral plow.\n\n**Weeping Soil (Recharge 5–6):**  \nThe Plowman slams his spectral plow into the ground. The earth in a 10-foot radius becomes soaked with cursed sorrow. All creatures within the area must succeed a **DC 13 Wisdom saving throw** or become **frightened** for 1 minute. A frightened creature may repeat the saving throw at the end of its turns.\n\n**Reap the Forgotten (1/day):**  \nThe Plowman whispers a name only the dead remember. One creature he can see must make a **DC 13 Constitution saving throw**. On a failure, the creature sees a vision of its own forgotten past or loss and takes **10 (3d6) psychic damage**, and is **stunned until the end of its next turn**. On a success, the target takes half damage and is not stunned.\n\n---\n\n### DEATH\n\nIf the Mourning Plowman is reduced to 0 HP _without having his name spoken or curse broken_, he releases a shriek of unimaginable sorrow that echoes through the Fields. All creatures within 30 feet must make a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw or be **haunted** (disadvantage on Insight and Perception) for the next long rest.\n\nIf his curse is broken peacefully, his spirit dissolves calmly into drifting wheat and ash, leaving behind a **Plowman's Token** — a carved bone talisman that grants **advantage on Survival checks made in cursed or haunted terrain**.","x":18280,"y":1358,"width":400,"height":781},
		{"id":"8b04529ac2693856","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.4 part 2  Fields of Misery.md","x":19500,"y":-420,"width":840,"height":1580},
		{"id":"bafc1cc525296ffd","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.5.6  The Statue-Island of the Drowned Shrines.md","x":20440,"y":1360,"width":560,"height":400},
