		{"id":"7c38807dd86a667d","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.5.7 Statue-Isle – The Drowned Shrines v2.md","x":21160,"y":1360,"width":540,"height":400},
		{"id":"a2f8efb50090dfa4","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.6 Troll Toll.md","x":21835,"y":-392,"width":825,"height":1532},
		{"id":"58fcc7a3c925d51b","type":"text","text":"Excellent. Let's give **Retchgut** a reward stash worth fighting for — and a dark secret or two to make this encounter even more layered.\n\n---\n\n## 💰 **Retchgut’s Treasure Hoard**\n\nHidden beneath the bridge, in a **slimy alcove behind a cracked support pillar**, the troll has stashed an assortment of **gleaming junk, rotten meat, and curious trinkets** looted from travelers, fallen adventurers, and unlucky scavengers.\n\n### 🧺 Contents of the Troll Hoard (Roll or Choose):\n\n1. **Rusting Warhammer** (worthless, except to a blacksmith — but the handle is hollow, and inside is a **silver ring** engraved with the symbol of Zakarum, worth **25 gp**).\n    \n2. **Small leather pouch** with **14 gp**, **8 sp**, and a single **obsidian eyeball** — warm to the touch (nonmagical, but unnerving).\n    \n3. A **sealed clay flask** labeled in faded Askari runes. Inside: **Distilled Bogrot** — a rare alchemical tonic that gives the drinker **advantage on Constitution saves** for 1 hour… and smells like fermented slug.\n    \n4. **Map Fragment**: One-quarter of a larger treasure map showing an unmarked ruin somewhere in the **Black Marsh**. Hints at “The Grave That Eats,” a side quest location.\n    \n5. **Swamp-Soaked Satchel** containing:\n    \n    - A **potion of greater healing**\n        \n    - A strange, **dried heart** wrapped in cloth — a **troll heart**. If consumed or boiled into a potion, grants **Regeneration (1 HP/round)** for 1 minute. One use only.\n        \n    - A handful of **tarnished silver teeth** (worth 10 gp total).\n        \n\n---\n\n## 🗝️ **Bridge Shortcut Key**\n\nTied to a piece of moldy sinew hanging from Retchgut’s belt is a **small, copper-plated emblem** in the shape of a **serpent wrapped around a willow branch**. This is a **pass token** once used by **swamp druids** to unlock hidden routes through the marshes.\n\n- With this token, the players can bypass the worst of the **bog traps** in the **Black Marsh**, reducing travel time and avoiding **one random encounter**.\n    \n- If identified, it’s also worth **50 gp to the right druid**… or can be used to **gain favor** with certain nature-based NPCs later.","x":21835,"y":1399,"width":400,"height":361,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c53a9c66720beff6","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.5.1 Sunken Chapel.md","x":20640,"y":-1520,"width":860,"height":900},
		{"id":"b54e6db8381ed7c8","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.5.2 Three Key Rooms Await.md","x":21660,"y":-1320,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"4ab4adf594ac0471","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.5.3 Chamber of the Spiral Oath (Puzzle Room).md","x":22340,"y":-1320,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"39f4cc20b0be97b1","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.5.4 The Reliquary of the Drowned Saint.md","x":22940,"y":-1320,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"0788920eb7f3af78","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.5.5 Crumbeling Encounter.md","x":23640,"y":-1320,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"ad108bc2f9e65298","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.2.1 - The Wither-Keeper.md","x":14760,"y":1680,"width":1060,"height":1237},
		{"id":"0609690d752054ee","type":"text","text":"### **Combat: Wither-Keeper**\n\n**Medium Undead (Fey-Touched), Chaotic Evil**  \n**Armor Class:** 13 (natural barkskin)  \n**Hit Points:** 62 (10d8+10)  \n**Speed:** 30 ft.\n\n**STR** 10 (+0)  \n**DEX** 14 (+2)  \n**CON** 12 (+1)  \n**INT** 15 (+2)  \n**WIS** 18 (+4)  \n**CHA** 10 (+0)\n\n**Saving Throws:** Wis +6, Con +3  \n**Damage Resistances:** necrotic, poison  \n**Condition Immunities:** charmed, frightened  \n**Senses:** darkvision 60 ft., passive Perception 14  \n**Languages:** Druidic, Common, Sylvan\n\n---\n\n### **Abilities:**\n\n- **Entangling Roots (Recharge 5–6):** The Wither-Keeper causes thorned roots to erupt in a 15-foot radius centered on himself. Creatures must succeed on a **DC 13 Strength saving throw** or be restrained for 1 minute. They can repeat the save at the end of each of their turns.\n    \n- **Bloodsap Touch (Melee Spell Attack):** +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature.  \n    Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) necrotic damage. The target also loses 1 hit point at the start of their next turn unless they use an action to cleanse the corruption.\n    \n- **Whispers of the Woods (1/day):** The Wither-Keeper targets one creature within 60 ft. that he can see. That creature must make a **DC 14 Wisdom saving throw** or be **haunted by voices**, taking disadvantage on all Wisdom-based checks and saving throws for 1 minute.\n    \n\n---\n\n### **Death Effect:**\n\nUpon defeat, the Wither-Keeper explodes into crawling vines and black spores. Any creature within 10 ft. must succeed a **DC 13 Constitution saving throw** or become **Poisoned for 1 hour**. In the writhing mass is a **Staff of Rotbark**:\n\n> **Rotbark Staff (Uncommon, requires attunement by a Druid or Warlock):**\n> \n> - Gain resistance to poison damage.\n>     \n> - 1/day: Cast _Entangle_ without using a spell slot.\n>     \n> - When wielded in both hands, deals 1d8 bludgeoning damage and counts as magical.\n>     \n> - Secret: If bathed in blood beneath a new moon, reveals a druidic map to the **Blighted Grove**, a hidden area related to Sanguinax’s past.\n>","x":14760,"y":3200,"width":1060,"height":1481,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"412bee56908e7cb0","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.1.1 Cold Plains - Iron Crypt.md","x":12520,"y":-1560,"width":730,"height":1042},
		{"id":"dfddce67d32a15ef","type":"text","text":"![[Pasted image 20250506172046.png]]\n","x":12678,"y":-2832,"width":684,"height":1042},
		{"id":"81afcde161972f5a","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.1.2 - Hall of Chains.md","x":14036,"y":-1560,"width":488,"height":1042},
		{"id":"2fb1b6678a6718db","type":"text","text":"minuut stilte","x":14155,"y":-1880,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"#ff00ff"},
		{"id":"742aefed67ffdff4","type":"text","text":"## 🐭 The Mimi Arc: “Roots Beneath the Fur”\n\n### 🖤 Overview\n\nMimi — Azure’s loyal pet mouse — unknowingly absorbed a fragment of the Root-Priest’s lingering essence during the fight at the Broken Tower. This fragment **buried itself deep** inside her tiny frame, **dormant at first**, but growing as they travel through the root-soaked lands of Khanduras.\n\nShe is now a **conduit** for ancient, fungal consciousness — and the perfect seedbed for **Alvex’s whispering will**.\n\n---\n\n## 🪰 Arc Timeline: Corruption Stages\n\nThese events unfold naturally over sessions as Azure journeys onward. You can space them by milestones or long rests.\n\n---\n\n### 🌱 STAGE 1 — “Patterns in the Dust” (Immediate)\n\n- Mimi scratches strange **spirals into the dirt** when Azure sleeps.\n    \n- Eevee hisses at her once and refuses to share Azure’s pouch.\n    \n- At night, Azure _hears whispering_, but cannot understand it. If she **casts Detect Thoughts** near Mimi, she hears a **repeating, childlike voice**:\n    \n    > “I miss the soil... I miss the root... I miss the fire...”\n    \n\n_No mechanical changes yet._\n\n---\n\n### 🌿 STAGE 2 — “Eyes in the Green” (After 2–3 major encounters)\n\n- Mimi’s eyes begin to glow faint **phosphorescent green** in the dark.\n    \n- She now **automatically detects nearby plant creatures** within 30 ft.\n    \n- When Azure uses elemental magic near Mimi, **roots twitch toward the source**.\n    \n\n_Azure must make a DC 13 WIS save when sleeping within 10 feet of Mimi or suffer unsettling dreams, gaining no benefit from long rest unless passed._\n\n---\n\n### 🌳 STAGE 3 — “She Speaks in Roots” (Mid-arc, after 1–2 more sessions)\n\n- Mimi begins to **speak** — softly, haltingly, in Whisper-tongue (understood only by Azure due to exposure).  \n    Phrases include:\n    \n    > “The Seed remembers you.”  \n    > “The girl in your blood smiles.”  \n    > “Alvex grows in your shadow.”\n    \n- Mimi can now **cast Entangle once per long rest**, centered on herself.\n    \n- She begins to **resist separation** from Azure, becoming anxious or violent when left behind.\n    \n\n---\n\n### 🌑 STAGE 4 — “Blooming Hunger” (Climax of the arc)\n\nMimi dies… but doesn’t.  \nHer body **blooms with white roots**, twisting into a strange skeletal creature — a **mouse-shaped root-golem** that floats slightly above the ground, her fur now moss and vine.\n\nThis transformation can be **delayed**, **hastened**, or **embraced** by Azure depending on her choices.\n\n---\n\n## 🌫️ Mimi the Root-Warden (Transformed Form) — Statblock\n\n**Tiny Elemental/Plant, Neutral (bonded to Azure)**\n\n> This is not a combat pet. It’s a **roleplay-focused creature** with narrative influence.\n\n---\n\n**Armor Class:** 15 (natural root armor)  \n**Hit Points:** 1 (but cannot be killed by physical damage; reforms over 24 hours unless purged)  \n**Speed:** 30 ft. hover\n\n---\n\n**Abilities:**\n\n- **Plant Empathy.** Detects emotions of plant/fungus creatures within 60 ft.\n    \n- **Root Flare.** Once per long rest, can cast _Faerie Fire_ (DEX DC 13).\n    \n- **Sporemind Channel.** Azure can use Mimi as a **focus** for spells requiring verbal components, even while silenced.\n    \n- **Alvex Fragment.** If Mimi is destroyed, Azure must make a **DC 15 CHA save** or be briefly possessed by the Root-Priest’s whispering voice — gaining **advantage on Insight**, but **disadvantage on Wisdom saves** for 1 hour.\n    \n\n---\n\n## 🧩 Moral & Narrative Dilemmas for Azure\n\nYou now have several great moments to tempt or torment Azure’s player:\n\n---\n\n### 🔥 Do you burn Mimi?\n\n- A strange druid in the mountains warns that the creature inside her is **“older than Sanctuary, and ten times more patient.”**\n    \n- A ritual can **burn the Root**, purifying her — but Azure must choose whether to **risk losing Mimi forever** or **keep the only familiar thing in a world that keeps getting darker.**\n    \n\n---\n\n### 🕯️ Do you join her to Alvex?\n\n- Azure may be able to **complete Mimi’s transformation**, creating a permanent companion bound to the Sporemind.\n    \n- This can come with **mechanical benefits**, like plant-based abilities, shared dreams, or influence over fungal/rot monsters.\n    \n- But it may also **mark Azure** — both magically and politically — as a servant of the Root.\n    \n\n---\n\n### ✨ Alternative Subplot Hooks\n\n- **The Whisperers of Leoric’s Hollow**, a group of **feral druids**, want to **harvest Mimi** for her seed.\n    \n- **The Echo Beneath** sends agents to retrieve “the last living seed of the Root-Priest,” believing Mimi is a **key to regenerating** one of their lost cult leaders.\n    \n- **Mimi’s dreams become maps**, pointing toward buried **sporemind relics** or forgotten Druid temples.\n    \n\n---\n\nWould you like a **player handout** or **prophetic dream scene** Azure could experience next to foreshadow this arc further?","x":11302,"y":-4480,"width":4518,"height":1144,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"58461b00ef49ab7c","type":"text","text":"moonlight amulet\nbag of holding\n","x":2880,"y":-1160,"width":250,"height":260,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"9515401a55cc135e","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 2 - Help the Rogue/Quest 2.1 - The loot.md","x":5120,"y":-2440,"width":520,"height":1280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c5512be438a6f3df","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 2 - Help the Rogue/Quest 2.2 - Banditcamp.md","x":6320,"y":-2240,"width":400,"height":880,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"07ff19a310380674","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 2 - Help the Rogue/Dialogue - Bandit camp guards.md","x":5680,"y":-3947,"width":485,"height":1427},
		{"id":"6032d003fe08c8a4","type":"text","text":"# Riddle\n\n> **Derrik (gruffly):**  \n> \"Hold up there, strangers. Hollow’s not a tavern you can just stumble into. Not unless you're lookin' to lose something.\"\n\n> **Marn (leans forward, a grin splitting his dirty face):**  \n> \"But... ==we’re feelin’ generous tonight. Ain’t that right, Derrik?\"==\n\n> **Derrik (snorts):**  \n> \"Generous, yeah. How about a game, then? A _riddle_. You solve it, you go in. You fail...\" _(he taps the haft of his weapon against the dirt)_ \"...well, we don’t bury what’s left.\"\n\n> **Marn (grinning wider):**  \n> \"Here it comes then. Listen close.\"\n\n---\n\n### ❓ The Riddle ❓\n\n> **Marn:**  \n> \"_I have no blade, yet I cut deep.  \n> I leave no mark, but make kings weep.  \n> I travel fast but make time slow—  \n> What am I?_\"\n\nIf the players say \"words\", \"a secret\", or \"a lie\", the guards nod approvingly.\n\n---\n\n> **Derrik (cracks his neck):**  \n> \"Hah. Looks like they got some brains to go with the blades.\"\n\n> **Marn:**  \n> \"Fine then. You lot can go through. Keep your weapons sheathed unless you want the Iron Bitch’s attention early.\"\n\n> _(He pulls a rope and the warped wooden gate creaks open, revealing the flickering firelight and smoke-choked tents within.)_\n\n> **Derrik (as they pass):**  \n> \"And if you _do_ see her... tell her Marn said she looked lovely last night.\" _(he laughs, and Marn punches his shoulder hard)_","x":6240,"y":-3947,"width":400,"height":1427},
		{"id":"1a5725f2d76593e9","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 2 - Help the Rogue/Quest 2.3.2 Treasure room.md","x":7200,"y":-3440,"width":400,"height":980,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"8199b1d68f6f16c0","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 2 - Help the Rogue/Quest 2.5 Puzzelkamer.md","x":8120,"y":-2440,"width":520,"height":1820,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"0dd04e9b6688ced7","type":"text","text":"# Party terug in Tristram naar Moreina\n\nGrote kans dat de party terugkomt na fight met Virella, Hier moeten we dialoog hebben van:\n\nIsabella - offering potatoes\n\nDe appotheker die nogmaals vraagt of ze z'n dochter en/of de heartroot gaan zoeken\n\nMoreina, die ze bedankt voor hun bijdragen en ze bij deze belooft te volgen tot het bittere einde <3\n\nBij een long rest moet mimi rare symptonen gaan vertonen (zie [[2.0.5.1 Overall implementation Mimi's revenge]] ) ","x":11302,"y":-980,"width":680,"height":640,"color":"#ff00ff"},
		{"id":"b81e76718494e86d","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Loot & Items/Loot - Windlash.md","x":2480,"y":-2300,"width":400,"height":950,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"181c3f4e19e7cc3b","type":"text","text":"### **The Shal'Zuun** (nieuwe tribe)\n\n_A name in an old tongue meaning “those who burn and rise.”_","x":3242,"y":-1270,"width":236,"height":340,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"79e6c963d16c7ee6","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 2 - Help the Rogue/Quest 2 - Dialogue Amazone.md","x":3640,"y":-1880,"width":400,"height":480,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d0a3b1cfa3b0a986","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 2 - Help the Rogue/Quest 2 - Help the Amazone.md","x":3640,"y":-1240,"width":400,"height":460,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"0d5cb800207bafdd","type":"text","text":"Niet helpen?","x":4133,"y":-960,"width":185,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"8f1ea18b87e6cbb9","type":"text","text":"# No entry\n\n_Two guards in piecemeal armor block the path, lit by the flicker of oil-drenched torches. The one with the halberd plants it in the dirt like a challenge. Neither looks impressed._\n\n> **Derrik (coldly):**  \n> \"Turn around. No one gets in the Hollow without the Iron Bitch’s say-so. And you don’t have it.\"\n\n> **Marn (leans on the gate, chewing something tough):**  \n> \"Don’t care who you are. Don’t care who you know. Even if your mother’s guts are strung up inside, _you’re not crossing this line._\"\n\n> **Derrik (spits at the ground):**  \n> \"Orders are orders. Vanya’s paranoid since the Askari showed up. Said if we let _anyone_ in without her word, she’d melt our faces down and wear 'em for kneecaps.\"\n\n> **Marn (shrugs):**  \n> \"Kinda believe her, too.\"\n\n> _(They don’t budge. The gate behind them stays barred. Smoke coils through the gaps in the palisade, and you hear the faint clang of steel—blacksmiths, or beatings, it’s hard to say.)_\n\n> **Derrik (more quietly, to himself):**  \n> \"...Though I _did_ hear the east gulley’s fence ain’t been fixed since the last storm... But that ain’t my business.\" _(he turns his back, pretending to scratch at something on his boot)_","x":5120,"y":-3947,"width":412,"height":660},
		{"id":"26b892b79b177628","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 3 - Help the Appocathary/Quest - Help the Apothecary 3.1.md","x":3560,"y":608,"width":402,"height":920,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f790e352b6a98890","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 3 - Help the Appocathary/Apothecary 3.2.md","x":4160,"y":608,"width":400,"height":920,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8d9c33f2a862064a","type":"text","text":"1. Bloodsap Dryads\n\nYou hear song—warped and mournful—echoing among the trees. Pale women, their skin etched with crimson veins, slide into view.\n“The pact must be honored. The Heartroot is not for the living. Leave, before the forest claims you too!”\n\nBattle or negotiate with 2–3 Bloodsap Dryads (statblocks as previously suggested).\nDiplomacy Option: Discovering one dryad’s sister is among the sick in Tristram gives them pause. \n\npenellope << zusje vcan dryad, ooit iets mee doen ?\n\ncalypso << naam dryad\n\n\n===Let @sybil shine, maybe she can ask the dryads talk with a little bit of magic===","x":4079,"y":1738,"width":562,"height":640,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"17b1f5e251d983a5","type":"text","text":"_\"My sister’s child suffers in Tristram. If you mean no harm, perhaps a token of goodwill could sway the forest’s judgment.\"_","x":4599,"y":2560,"width":323,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"8065916e35fca3a9","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 3 - Help the Appocathary/Apothecary 3.3.md","x":4760,"y":608,"width":520,"height":1092,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"13d003765c6f4233","type":"text","text":"**Possible Rewards**\n\nHeartroot Herb (restores hit points and ends magical diseases/curses).\nFavors or relics from the apothecary.\nLirael’s gratitude: a blessing, secret lore, or a ghostly aid in a coming battle.\nFurther Adventure Seeds","x":5571,"y":3177,"width":360,"height":640,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"8df09b8213a41bf2","type":"text","text":"<<<< Not defeated, he flees into thin air, as if he dissolves in ashes and dust and returns later as a massive fuck all fuck off demon\n","x":6396,"y":2640,"width":250,"height":240,"color":"#ff00ff"},
		{"id":"c30b06a4d82cec5a","type":"text","text":"### Sanguinax Spawn (Lesser Blood Demon)\n\n_Small fiend, chaotic evil_\n\n- **Armor Class:** 15 (natural armor)\n- **Hit Points:** 36 (8d6+8)\n- **Speed:** 30 ft., fly 30 ft.\n\n| STR | DEX | CON | INT | WIS | CHA |  \n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |  \n| 14 (+2) | 16 (+3) | 13 (+1) | 8 (-1) | 10 (+0) | 12 (+1) |\n\n**Skills:** Stealth +5  \n**Damage Resistances:** Cold; Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing from nonmagical attacks  \n**Damage Immunities:** Necrotic  \n**Senses:** Darkvision 60 ft., Passive Perception 10  \n**Languages:** Abyssal, Telepathy 30 ft.\n\n**Traits:**\n\n- **Blood Lash (Melee Weapon Attack):** +5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) necrotic damage and target must succeed on DC 13 Constitution saving throw or bleed, taking 3 (1d6) necrotic damage at the start of its turns for 1 minute.\n- **Flyby:** The demon doesn’t provoke opportunity attacks when flying out of an enemy's reach.\n- **Blood Spray (Recharge 5-6):** The demon releases a spray of blood in a 15 ft. cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a DC 14 Dexterity saving throw or take 14 (4d6) necrotic damage and is blinded until the end of its next turn.","x":5849,"y":2220,"width":455,"height":791,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c0cdb4ced1b0bdf0","type":"text","text":"```encounter\nname: Encounter\nplayers:\n  - Bo\n  - Sybil\n  - Azura Nexendis\ncreatures:\n  - \"1\": Ghost\n```\n","x":5321,"y":2509,"width":345,"height":502,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"f407b2b777a4b20e","type":"file","file":"Main Story/NPC Lore/Wirt the Scrollmonger.md","x":3960,"y":-660,"width":800,"height":540},
		{"id":"cb9f819a8df8e322","type":"text","text":"**Harland, Watch Captain of Tristram**  \n_(arms crossed, brow furrowed as he spots the party readying at the gates)_  \n“Leaving already? Hmph. You barely look like you've survived a tavern brawl, let alone the road to that cursed cathedral. The Black Marsh isn’t kind to the unprepared.”\n\n_(he pauses, his eyes catching a faint **golden shimmer** leaking from the bag of holding — his sternness flickers into something warmer)_  \n“Wait... that glow. Is that what I think it is?”  \n_(he steps closer, voice low and laced with a rare flicker of hope)_  \n“You’ve got a level-up potion, don’t you?”\n\n_(he glances between them, the weight of unspoken losses in his tone)_  \n“If ever there was a time to drink it, it’s now. Whatever lies ahead in that cathedral... it won’t show mercy. And neither should you.”","x":11279,"y":885,"width":446,"height":795},
		{"id":"2ec5731050ec3848","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.8.1 glass to know one.md","x":23640,"y":1360,"width":680,"height":1800},
		{"id":"24222b2baf37bf53","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.7 Black Marsh.md","x":22180,"y":-4640,"width":760,"height":1561},
		{"id":"4f85812bfb31c286","type":"text","text":"Opties\n","x":22435,"y":-4760,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"039f2c5a7ad4b9da","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.8  Black marsh option 2.md","x":22900,"y":-392,"width":800,"height":1532},
		{"id":"3f3e27807e0f5efc","type":"text","text":"## **The Hollow Knight**\n\n_Medium undead, lawful neutral_\n\n**Armor Class** 18 (rusted plate)  \n**Hit Points** 142 (15d8 + 75)  \n**Speed** 25 ft. (10 ft. in deep water)\n\n|STR|DEX|CON|INT|WIS|CHA|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|18 (+4)|12 (+1)|20 (+5)|10 (+0)|14 (+2)|12 (+1)|\n\n**Saving Throws** Con +8, Wis +5  \n**Skills** Athletics +7, Perception +5  \n**Damage Resistances** bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing from nonmagical attacks  \n**Damage Immunities** poison, necrotic  \n**Condition Immunities** charmed, frightened, poisoned, exhaustion  \n**Senses** darkvision 60 ft., passive Perception 15  \n**Languages** Common, Zakarum (ancient dialect)  \n**Challenge** 8 (3,900 XP)\n\n---\n\n### **Traits**\n\n**Spectral Reach.** The Hollow Knight’s halberd attacks have a reach of 10 ft. They can also strike through solid surfaces up to 1 inch thick.\n\n**Aura of Drain.** Any creature that starts its turn within 10 ft. of the Hollow Knight must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have its movement speed reduced by 5 ft. until the end of its next turn. This effect stacks up to a maximum reduction of 15 ft.\n\n**Swamp Stride.** The Hollow Knight ignores movement penalties caused by difficult terrain in the marsh.\n\n---\n\n### **Actions**\n\n**Multiattack.** The Hollow Knight makes two halberd attacks.\n\n**Halberd.** _Melee Weapon Attack:_ +7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target.  \nHit: 14 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage.\n\n**Spectral Slam (Recharge 5–6).** The Hollow Knight slams the halberd’s butt into the ground, creating a wave of necrotic force. Each creature in a 15–ft. radius must make a DC 16 Constitution saving throw, taking 27 (6d8) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success. Creatures reduced to 0 HP this way rise 1 round later as **Swamp Husks** under the Hollow Knight’s control (AC 13, HP 9).\n\n---\n\n### **Legendary Actions** _(Optional for harder fight)_\n\nThe Hollow Knight can take 2 legendary actions, choosing from the options below.\n\n- **Detect.** Makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n    \n- **Halberd Strike.** Makes one halberd attack.\n    \n- **Drain Pulse (Costs 2 Actions).** Forces all creatures within 10 ft. to make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or suffer -10 ft. movement until the end of their next turn.","x":25100,"y":-1320,"width":680,"height":740},
		{"id":"2267ae7b6d43ec08","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 4 - Road to Cathedral/4.10 The Weeping Gate.md","x":25840,"y":-392,"width":700,"height":1552},
		{"id":"4f3542df9991c8fd","type":"text","text":"## **Cathedral of Tristram – Exterior Description**\n\nThe path through the Black Marsh ends abruptly at a cracked stone courtyard, its flagstones half-swallowed by black moss and skeletal weeds. Beyond it, the **Cathedral of Tristram** looms like a wounded beast — its once-proud spires now jagged stumps, struck by time, storm, and some greater violence.\n\nThe main doors are massive slabs of blackened oak, banded with iron that is eaten through by rust. A faint **red light pulses** between the seams of the wood, as though the building itself breathes. All around the façade, the stonework is etched with ancient, crumbling carvings — angels whose faces are worn smooth, warriors with broken swords, and beasts that look disturbingly alive when caught in the corner of your vision.\n\nAbove the door, a circular stained-glass window depicts a crowned figure holding a scepter — but the crown has cracked in the glass, the missing shards leaving a gaping hole where the face should be.\n\nThe air is bitter here, carrying the faint smell of ash and something far older — the scent of a grave long-forgotten.","x":24997,"y":-151,"width":683,"height":704},
		{"id":"388dea5b35d96be6","type":"text","text":"### **Narrative Transition**\n\nAs the Hollow Knight collapses, his armor falls in on itself like an empty shell, the halberd dissolving into black mist that seeps into the earth. The stagnant marsh water slowly recedes from the stone path ahead, revealing a broken causeway that leads toward higher ground.\n\nThrough the drifting fog, the jagged silhouette of the Cathedral rises in the distance — its spire fractured, its stained-glass windows shattered, and a faint, malevolent red glow leaking from within.\n\nBehind you, the Black Marsh seems to grow silent, as though the land itself is holding its breath. Ahead, every step toward the Cathedral feels heavier, the air colder.\n\n**The doors to the Cathedral are now within reach.**","x":26700,"y":-60,"width":693,"height":573},
		{"id":"679ba43bc09f6a04","type":"file","file":"Main Story/Story/Quest 5 - Cathedral/5.0 Cathedral Entrance.md","x":27640,"y":-280,"width":845,"height":941},
